msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00613"
msgid ""
"A subtype of idiopathic generalized epilepsy characterized by onset "
"occurring around puberty, absence seizures, generalized tonic-clonic "
"seizures (GTCS), GTCS on awakening, and myoclonic seizures."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00614"
msgid ""
"A subtype of idiopathic generalized epilepsy. Patients have afebrile "
"seizures only, with onset in adolescence (rather than in childhood) and "
"myoclonic jerks which usually occur after awakening and are triggered by "
"sleep deprivation and fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00615"
msgid ""
"A subtype of idiopathic generalized epilepsy. Patients have afebrile "
"seizures only, with onset in adolescence (rather than in childhood) and "
"myoclonic jerks which usually occur after awakening and are triggered by "
"sleep deprivation and fatigue."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00616"
msgid ""
"A neurodegenerative disorder which is closely related to but clinically "
"distinct from amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. It is a progressive paralytic "
"disorder which results from dysfunction of the upper motor neurons while the"
" lower neurons are unaffected."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00617"
msgid ""
"A disorder characterized by absent or incomplete sexual maturation by the "
"age of 18 years, in conjunction with low levels of circulating gonadotropins"
" and testosterone and no other abnormalities of the hypothalamic-pituitary "
"axis. In some cases, it is associated with non- reproductive phenotypes, "
"such as anosmia, cleft palate, and sensorineural hearing loss. Anosmia or "
"hyposmia is related to the absence or hypoplasia of the olfactory bulbs and "
"tracts. Hypogonadism is due to deficiency in gonadotropin-releasing hormone "
"and probably results from a failure of embryonic migration of gonadotropin- "
"releasing hormone-synthesizing neurons. In the presence of anosmia, "
"idiopathic hypogonadotropic hypogonadism is referred to as Kallmann "
"syndrome, whereas in the presence of a normal sense of smell, it has been "
"termed normosmic idiopathic hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (nIHH)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "model:gnuhealth.protein.disease,description:DI-00618"
msgid ""
"A disorder characterized by absent or incomplete sexual maturation by the "
